	(descr "Horizontal-mount axial film capacitor, body 34.0mm long x 22.5mm diameter, lead diameter 1.0mm, pin pitch 40.00mm. Drawn 2026-07-29 for Cornell Dubilier (Knowles) Type 942C part 942C16P1K-F, 0.10uF / 1600Vdc / 460Vac. Body dimensions are the datasheet's own 'Ratings and Dimensions' row, read from CDE catalog 942C.pdf (https://www.cde.com/resources/catalogs/942C.pdf) printed page 2, 1600 Vdc block: '.10 | 942C16P1K-F | D 22.5 | L 34.0 | d 1.0'; corroborated in CDE's older sheet PULSE-942C.pdf, which prints the same row in inches ('.887 (22.5)' x '1.339 (34.0)', d '.040 (1.0)'). D and L are catalogue MAXIMA -- CDE prints 'L MAX.' and 'D MAX.' on the mechanical drawing -- so the body outline here is a worst-case envelope, not a nominal. Pin pitch 40.00mm = 34.0mm body + 3.0mm lead-forming allowance per side, matching the KiCad stock C_Axial/CP_Axial family convention (2.5-3.25mm per side across L30.0/P35.00, L22.0/P27.50 and L34.5/P41.00). CDE's drawing specifies 1.625in (41mm) MIN free lead each side, so 3.0mm of formed lead is available with a very large margin. Hole 1.3mm = 1.0mm lead + 0.3mm IPC-2222 Level-B clearance; pad 2.6mm gives a 0.65mm annular ring, wider than the KiCad stock C_Axial default (drill+0.8) because this land carries ~7A rms continuously in the resonant tank -- see docs/evidence/2026-07-29-tank-cap-cde-942c-verification.md. Non-polarised: pad 1 is drawn roundrect for orientation reference only, the part has no polarity.")
